   "history": "Kibbeh (also called Niter Kibbeh — 'spiced butter') is the second great foundation of Ethiopian cooking — alongside berbere, it is used in virtually every Ethiopian dish. Clarified butter infused with a carefully chosen blend of aromatics (onion, garlic, ginger, turmeric, cardamom, cinnamon, and rue), kibbeh carries these flavours into every dish it cooks. Unlike Indian ghee (which is pure clarified butter with no additions), kibbeh is a compound spiced butter that simultaneously provides the cooking fat and the aromatic base of the dish."
