   "history": "Tigray is the northernmost highland region of Ethiopia — the heartland of the ancient Aksumite civilisation (1st—7th century CE) that was one of the world's first Christian kingdoms. Tigrayan cuisine (called Tigrinya cuisine) is closely related to Eritrean food and uses similar ingredients to the broader Ethiopian tradition but with distinctive preparation methods. Tsebhi (the Tigrinya word for wat) is made with more acidity (from tamarind or dried lemon) and a specific spice blend called Berbere Tigrinya that differs from standard berbere. Birsen means lentils — Tsebhi Birsen is the Tigrayan lentil wat."
