  "desc": "GieesK Ethiopian Heritage Platter — the complete Ethiopian culinary journey: the Coffee Ceremony (ETH211), the Grand Beyaynetu (ETH140), Doro Wat (ETH061), Key Wat (ETH021), Kitfo (ETH029), Tigrayan Tihlo (ETH236), Gurage Kitfo (ETH237), Tej (ETH215), Honey Cake (ETH199), and Coffee Cheesecake (ETH287). Three thousand years of Ethiopian food culture on one grand table.",
  "longDesc": "The GieesK Ethiopian Heritage Platter is the ultimate expression of our commitment to Ethiopian food culture — assembling the complete spectrum from ancient to modern, from highland to lowland, from fasting to feast, in a grand celebration that honours the depth and diversity of one of the world's great culinary civilizations.\n\nThis is not just a meal — it is an education, a celebration, and a statement. Ethiopia gave the world coffee. Ethiopia produced the most extensive plant-based food tradition in history. Ethiopia created injera, berbere, kitfo, and the coffee ceremony. This platter is the full expression of that heritage.\n\nThe GieesK Heritage Platter is our signature: 300 recipes, one country, one heritage.",
