  "desc": "Kenyan Beef Pilau is a fragrant, deeply spiced one-pot rice dish that stands as one of the country's most celebrated recipes. Tender beef, deeply caramelised onions, basmati rice, and a hand-ground blend of cumin, cardamom, cloves, cinnamon, and pepper all come together into something that smells like a celebration.",
  "longDesc": "Pilau has a long and storied history on the Kenyan coast, shaped by centuries of Indian Ocean trade that brought Persian, Indian, and Arab culinary traditions to East Africa. Over generations it became embraced across the entire country and is now the centrepiece of weddings, Eid, Christmas, birthdays, and family gatherings from Mombasa to Nairobi. The defining element is patience — deeply browned onions, toasted whole spices ground fresh, and rice that is never stirred while it cooks.",
