  "desc": "Samaki wa Kupaka is the jewel of Kenya's Swahili coast — a whole fish scored, marinated in garlic, ginger, and lemon, grilled over charcoal until smoky and tender, then coated in a rich, golden coconut milk sauce fragrant with turmeric, coriander, and chilli. A dish that tastes of the Indian Ocean.",
  "longDesc": "From Mombasa to Lamu, Samaki wa Kupaka tells the story of the Swahili coast in a single dish — centuries of Arab, Persian, and Indian Ocean trade woven into every spoonful of coconut sauce. The technique of grilling the fish first over charcoal before bathing it in coconut milk is the defining move: the smoke of the grill and the richness of the coconut create a flavour combination that is entirely, unmistakably coastal Kenyan.",
