   "note": "Mandazi and Mahamri are often confused but are distinct recipes. Mandazi uses baking powder and has a denser, firmer crumb, while Mahamri uses yeast giving it a lighter, airier texture and a richer coconut flavour. Mahamri puffs more dramatically during frying and is the more traditional coastal celebration bread. Mandazi is the quicker, everyday nationwide favourite."
