  "desc": "Kuku wa Nazi is the jewel of Swahili coastal cooking — chicken slowly simmered in creamy coconut milk with onions, tomatoes, garlic, ginger, and warm spices until the sauce is rich, golden, and deeply fragrant. Always served with Wali wa Nazi. Always celebrated.",
  "longDesc": "There is a reason Kuku wa Nazi is prepared for every important occasion along the Kenyan coast — weddings, Eid, family homecomings. The combination of chicken simmering in coconut milk with turmeric, coriander, and garlic creates something that is simultaneously comforting and festive. The sauce turns a deep gold, thick and fragrant, clinging to every piece of chicken. Set it next to a bowl of Wali wa Nazi and you have one of the great meal combinations in all of Kenyan cuisine.",
