   "history": "Terere — amaranth greens — is one of the oldest cultivated and wild-harvested leafy vegetables in Kenya. For generations, families across Western Kenya, Nyanza, the Rift Valley, and Central Kenya have gathered or grown terere in their homestead gardens, preparing it as a simple, quick side dish alongside ugali, stew, or other staples. It is a food of both agricultural tradition and everyday practicality — fast to prepare, deeply nutritious, and available throughout the year.",
