   "origin": "Lake Victoria basin — Luo and Luhya fishing communities",
   "history": "Tilapia from Lake Victoria has fed East African communities for thousands of years. The Luo and Luhya people of the lake basin developed fishing as a central part of their culture and economy. Fried tilapia — crispy-skinned, whole or in fillets — became Kenya's most beloved fish preparation, spreading far beyond the lake to restaurants and homes across the entire country.",
