   "origin": "Mombasa, Kenyan Swahili Coast — centuries of Arab, Persian, and Indian Ocean culinary influence",
   "history": "Mombasa pilau is considered the original and most authentic version of Kenyan pilau. Brought to the Swahili coast through Indian Ocean trade routes, it has been refined over centuries in the Old Town kitchens of Mombasa into the deeply aromatic, caramelised-onion-forward dish that defines Kenyan celebration cooking. Every wedding, Eid feast, and important gathering along the coast centres around a large pot of Mombasa pilau.",
