   "history": "Mursik is the sacred fermented milk of the Maasai and Kalenjin peoples. Prepared in a calabash gourd treated with charcoal from specific trees, the milk ferments slowly over 1—3 days. The charcoal imparts a distinctive smoky, slightly bitter character that is the defining flavour of authentic mursik. It has sustained Maasai pastoralist communities for thousands of years and remains deeply embedded in cultural ceremonies, celebrations, and daily life.",
