   "history": "Kuku wa Kupaka is perhaps Tanzania's most distinctive dish — whole chicken marinated in Zanzibar spices, grilled over charcoal, then repeatedly basted with a rich coconut-tamarind sauce as it cooks. The result is a deeply lacquered, fragrant, slightly charred chicken unlike anything else in East African cooking. \"Kupaka\" means \"to smear\" or \"to apply\" — the process of basting the coconut sauce is the soul of the dish.",
