   "history": "Kashata is one of the oldest sweets of the Swahili coast — made from grated coconut and sugar cooked together until the mixture caramelises and sets into firm, sweet squares. It has been made in Zanzibar's homes and sold at its markets for centuries. The version with peanuts is equally beloved; the pink-tinted version using rose water or hibiscus is particularly festive."
