   "history": "Chips Mayai is Tanzania's most beloved and original street food creation — a thick omelette made by pouring beaten eggs over a pan of freshly fried chips, pressing everything together until the egg sets around the chips. The result is a square of crispy chips bound in fluffy egg — filling, affordable, and completely irreplaceable. It is sold at every chips stand in every Tanzanian city and town, made to order in the same heavy steel pans that have been in use for decades. No other country has this dish."
