   "history": "The Chaga (Wachaga) are the Bantu people who farm the fertile volcanic slopes of Kilimanjaro — Africa's highest mountain. Their land produces some of Tanzania's finest bananas, and their cuisine is built almost entirely around the banana in every stage of ripeness: green for soup and stew, partially ripe for cooking, fully ripe for eating and fermenting. Banana soup (made from boiled green bananas with beans and greens) is one of the oldest Chaga preparations and reflects the remarkable nutritional wisdom of a people who built a complete diet around one crop.",
