   "history": "Mbege is the sacred banana beer of the Chaga people — fermented from ripe bananas and eleusine (finger millet), it is the drink of every significant Chaga ceremony. Weddings, funerals, naming ceremonies, elder meetings, and harvest celebrations all begin and end with mbege. It is offered to ancestral spirits, shared between families to seal agreements, and given to elders as the highest form of respect. The brewing of mbege is traditionally a skill passed from mother to daughter."
