   "history": "The Sukuma (WaSukuma) are Tanzania's largest ethnic group, numbering over 10 million people, living primarily around the southern shore of Lake Victoria. Their cuisine is built around the extraordinary protein resources of the lake — Nile perch (sangara), tilapia, and dagaa — and their staple ugali. Dried fish (particularly dried sangara) is preserved for the months between fishing seasons and reconstituted in thick tomato-based stews that are eaten with stiff ugali. This is the daily meal of millions of Tanzanians."
