   "history": "The Gogo (Wagogo) people inhabit the central plateau of Tanzania around Dodoma — one of the driest, most challenging environments in the country. Their ecology has shaped a cuisine built around extreme drought resilience: sorghum, finger millet, groundnuts, and cattle. The Gogo are also renowned across Tanzania for their music — the traditional tunes (nyimbo za Wagogo) are among the country's most distinctive. Gogo food reflects their environment: simple, nourishing, and built to sustain people through drought. The combination of sorghum ugali with thick groundnut sauce is the Gogo's most fundamental meal."
