   "history": "The Iraqw (Wairaqw) are a Cushitic-speaking people of the Mbulu Highlands near Lake Manyara — linguistically related to peoples of Ethiopia and the Horn of Africa rather than the surrounding Bantu and Nilotic groups. Their Cushitic heritage is reflected in their food culture, which places a much stronger emphasis on fermented milk than typical Bantu East African cuisine. The Iraqw keep cattle and goats and their fermented milk traditions are sophisticated, producing a variety of soured milk products that are consumed daily."
