  "desc": "Tanzania — A Culinary Journey. 300 recipes. 120+ ethnic groups. The Kilimanjaro slopes and the Zanzibar coast. The Serengeti plains and the Makonde plateau. The ancient Hadzabe and the modern Dar es Salaam café. This is everything Tanzania tastes like.",
  "longDesc": "Tanzania's 300 recipes on GieesK are a journey through the most culinarily diverse country in East Africa — a nation of 120+ ethnic groups, a coastline shaped by a thousand years of Indian Ocean trade, highlands of remarkable agricultural ingenuity, and a food culture that is simultaneously ancient and urgently contemporary. This entry celebrates the completion of the Tanzania collection and serves as the entry point for anyone who wants to understand Tanzania through its food.\n\nThe journey begins at TZA001 (Ugali — the national staple) and ends here at TZA300. Between these two points: the fire of pili pili and the gentleness of vitumbua; the ancient patience of Zanzibar halwa and the modern confidence of the craft burger; the Hadzabe hunter's fire and the Zanzibar hotel's finest kitchen; the Chaga coffee ceremony and the cold brew tangawizi. This is Tanzania.",
